{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי יד", :translit "ki yad", :gloss "for the hand"} {:he "יו\"ד של כי", :translit "yod shel ki", :gloss "the yod of ki"} {:he "יד", :translit "yad", :gloss "hand"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "יו\"ד של כי ויד", :b "דויד"}], :frame {:text "In Exodus 17:16 Moses declares that the battle against Amalek is conducted 'because a hand is on the throne of YHWH.' The Talmud interprets this oath as a pledge that God wages war against Amalek 'from generation to generation'; Moses himself is understood as having taken this oath. By encoding David into the opening words, Ba'al HaTurim connects this oath to the future king appointed to fulfill it.", :sources ["Megillah 18a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מדר דר", :translit "mid dor dor", :gloss "from generation to generation"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מדר דר", :b "לימי משיח"}], :frame {:text "The verse Exodus 17:16 describes the ongoing war against Amalek fought 'from generation to generation' (מדר דר). The Talmud identifies this verse as the scriptural source for the obligation to remember what Amalek did, an obligation tied to the messianic era when Amalek's name is ultimately eradicated.", :sources ["Megillah 18a" "Deuteronomy 25:19"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "יו\"ד של כי ויד", :a-value 400, :b "דויד", :b-value 24, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "מדר דר", :a-value 448, :b "לימי משיח", :b-value 448, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:16:57.320968058Z", :model "glm-5.2"}